# Tracer: ordinary piecewise definitions retain and project all successful checks.
# Before (same source verified, but disjointness returned only bool):
# have fn choose(x R) R by cases:
#     case x < 0: x
#     case x >= 0: x + 1
# Now: coverage, each disjoint pair and each return check retain scoped evidence.
# Boundary: overlapping branches and a branch with 1 / 0 remain rejected.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -lang en -strict -f examples/stmt_nodes/definition/have_fn_cases_evidence.lit

have fn choose(x R) R by cases:
    case x < 0: x
    case x >= 0: x + 1
